Agentis AI Frameworks:
No framework  -> MCP (opensource protocol) -> OpenAI Agents SDK -> Crew AI -> LangGraph (LangChain) -> AutoGen (Microsoft)




MCP - It is an open-source standard designed to connect AI models (like Gemini, ChatGPT, or Claude) directly to external data sources, applications, and developer tools.

Arch/components:
Host - host is the application that user interacts with => IDE, desktop chat applications
Client - MCP client lives in the Host application.Client converts the AI intentions to structured protocol messages.communicateds with MCP servers and send request and receive response 
server - lightweight program that exposes the capabilities to the AI system

A server can provide:

tools/functions => Tools are executable functions.(run SQL query, send slack msg etc.,) - Give an LLM power to carry out actions like 
resources/documents => Resources are read-only or contextual data sources. (files, doc, logs etc) fetched not executed
prompts/templates => 
workflows

